 "notes": "Koh Bida Nok, the outer of the two Bida limestone islets 2 km south of Phi Phi Leh; coastlines of Bida Nok and Bida Nai from OpenStreetMap. Cave, swim-through, coral heads and depths; the sheltered bay, Finger Reef and the leopard-shark sand from Phuket Dive Guide. The wall runs from the waterline to sand at 20-25 m; the usual dive circles the island. Positions are approximate.",
